<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What may leave this device in a backup. Applies below API 31; see
    data_extraction_rules.xml for 31 and above.

    The device's identity, its catalog and its blocks live in `no_backup` and
    are excluded by the platform, which is why they are kept there: restoring a
    device identity onto a second phone would put two members of the mesh behind
    one id and one certificate.

    `files/sync` is excluded here for a related reason. It holds the files this
    device is recorded as a holder of, and the record lives in the database that
    is not backed up - so restoring the files alone would produce a phone
    holding bytes that no catalog anywhere says it has. Pairing and pulling are
    how a replacement device gets its files, and they keep the catalog honest
    while doing it.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="file" path="sync" />
</full-backup-content>
